      "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #62848. DeepSeek-OCR and Unlimited-OCR fail to start on v0.32.0 because the DeepEncoder rel-pos attention kernel added in #55629 reads `LOG2E`, a plain Python float, from inside `@triton.jit`, and Triton 3.7 rejects non-constexpr globals.\n\n## Claims\n\n- DeepSeek-OCR starts and serves again on v0.32.0 / main (Triton 3.7.1).\n- Adds the first test for `deepencoder_rel_pos_attention`, which compares it with the non-Triton path.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test, `pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_deepencoder_rel_pos_attention.py` (float16 and bfloat16, 8x8, 14x14 and 16x12 grids), on an RTX 5060 Ti (SM120) with torch 2.13.0+cu130 and Triton 3.7.1:\n- v0.32.0: 6 failed, each with the `CompilationError` from the issue\n- this PR: 6 passed\n\nEnd to end, `LLM(\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-OCR\", enable_prefix_caching=False, mm_processor_cache_gb=0, enforce_eager=True)` with a rendered image and the prompt `<image>\\nFree OCR.` at temperature 0:\n- v0.32.0: `Engine core initialization failed`, with the `NameError(\"Cannot access global variable LOG2E from within @jit'ed function ...\")` from the issue\n- this PR: `'Invoice 2026-10-21\\n\\nTotal due: 1,234.56 EUR\\n\\nThank you for your order'`, which matches the image\n\n`ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on the changed files.\n\n## Details\n\nThe fix wraps the same value in `tl.constexpr` next to the kernel, as `gumbel.py` does for `_TL_RAND_MIN`. `vllm.triton_utils.LOG2E` stays a float, because `xpu_mla_sparse.py` uses it in host code (`sm_scale *= LOG2E`). This kernel is the only `@triton.jit` code that reads it. The `TritonLanguagePlaceholder` maps `tl.constexpr` to the identity, so importing the model without Triton still works.\n\nNot a duplicate: no open PR mentions #62848, DeepEncoder or this constant. The issue's side note about `NGramPerReqLogitsProcessor` and the V2 model runner is a separate problem and isn't changed here.\n\nAI assistance was used: I used Claude Code to reproduce the failure, write the fix and test, and run the validation above. I reviewed every changed line.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
