                  "body": "I checked the other kernels on main, and this is the only one that reads `triton_utils.LOG2E` as a global inside `@triton.jit`. `rocm_aiter_mla_merge.py` and `xpu_mla_sparse.py` pass `LOGE2` in as a `tl.constexpr` kernel argument (`LOGE2=LOGE2` at launch), so Triton 3.7 accepts them. `fast_exp` in mamba's `triton_helpers.py` defines its own `tl.constexpr` inside the function. `xpu_mla_sparse.py` also uses `LOG2E` in host code (`sm_scale *= LOG2E`), which is why I left the shared value as a plain float.\r\n\r\nIf you'd rather match the other kernels, I can pass `LOG2E` in as a `tl.constexpr` argument here instead of the module-level `_LOG2E`.\r\n",
